 having kids it's so easy  to give parenting advice so  you tell me damon how if i'm way off  base here but i feel like as a parent  you have to be willing to let your kids  fail a little bit so what i mean by that  is  i grew up like my dad was a very strict  christian father so i had these  boundaries that i was constantly  crossing that he had set because they  were a little bit too extreme  my mom was on the other side where she  gave me no boundaries so i had to kind  of discover you know what my boundaries  were with her  um but yeah what do you think about that  as far as like how  what can we tell parents to help them  maybe be okay with like  letting their kids fail a little bit and  discovering those boundaries  on their own so you know there is no  perfect parenting book because every  child is different you mean your book  isn't the perfect parenting book it's  really close  in fact what i try to do is i i try to  talk  in terms of concepts parenting concepts  these are the big picture things because  to apply it to individual children if i  say this is the best way to do this  it really depends on your child on their  temperament and their experiences  because you're right every boundary can  be crossed in a different way and you  can't predict and anticipate  every single way right so so yeah it  really depends on  on the way your child's going to turn  and then you fall back on the basics  you know what's the big picture here why  am i upset  and fall back on that because if you can  model big picture thinking when you're  dealing with  that's it i'm taking away your phone for  the next three weeks well  you know just because they swore at me  is that really worth taking away their  phone or through  maybe they swarmed me because they're  really mad at me and maybe there's a  reason for them to be mad you know you  have to step back and see the big  picture  um but yeah they'll cross boundaries you  never even knew existed

